# BMW X5 E70 five-door SUV, 2007-2013.
#
# The second X5: the larger and wider body, the curved roofline, the
# twin-kidney grille and the split tailgate. UK sales from 28 April 2007.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BMW_X5_(E70)
#
# Dimensions 4.854 x 1.933 x 1.766-1.776 m, wheelbase 2.933 m.
#
# Shape reference: NO true level side profile exists. Image 1 is a
# facelifted car; the two 3.0d quarter views are pre-facelift. The flank is
# estimated from them within the published dimensions; the mismatch is
# recorded.
#
# Colours: grade (c), provisional. Black, silver, white and blue are plain
# names. Weights 20, 18, 17, 15, total 70, provisional.
#
# Speed 210 km/h. Comfort 95/473, on the line 330 + 1.5 x 95. Class 3.
# Dates are road presence: 2007 intro, retires staggered 2027-2030.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/bmw-x5-e70.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/bmw-x5-e70.dae. References:
# citycars/references/bmw-x5-e70/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: image 1 is a facelifted car and was used only for the
# flank; the pre-facelift nose and tail come from images 2-3. The lower intake,
# rear lamp wrap and split-tailgate detailing are simplified. At 128 px the wider
# body and curved roofline read as an E70 X5.


obj=citycar
name=BMWX5E70(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=20
intro_year=2007
intro_month=4
retire_year=2030
retire_month=6
speed=210
class=3
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=95
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=473

